WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.068
Better learning design begins with performance.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:06.004
What should learners be able to do after the course that they

00:00:06.004 --> 00:00:07.644
could not do reliably before?

00:00:07.644 --> 00:00:10.924
Once that outcome is clear, the objective, examples, practice, feedback,

00:00:10.924 --> 00:00:13.876
and assessment can all point in the same direction.

00:00:13.876 --> 00:00:17.484
If the goal is decision quality, the course should include decisions.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:21.420
If the goal is procedure accuracy, the course should include procedural practice.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.684
If the goal is judgment, the course should expose learners to realistic tradeoffs.

00:00:25.684 --> 00:00:26.340
Sequencing matters.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.292
Learners often benefit from concrete examples before abstract rules,

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:32.900
simple cases before complex ones, and guided practice before independent performance.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.820
Summaries and reflection help learners consolidate what they noticed and connect it to future use.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.756
Feedback loops help them improve while there is still time to adjust.

00:00:41.756 --> 00:00:47.004
Assessment alignment keeps the course honest by measuring the capability the instruction was supposed to build.

00:00:47.004 --> 00:00:48.972
Good design also avoids information dumps.

00:00:48.972 --> 00:00:51.268
More content is not automatically more learning.

00:00:51.268 --> 00:00:55.204
A course can be comprehensive and still be structured, focused, and usable.

00:00:55.204 --> 00:00:59.140
Inclusive and accessible design strengthens learning by reducing unnecessary barriers and making

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.764
participation more reliable across different learners and environments.

00:01:01.764 --> 00:01:03.732
The aim is not passive completion.

00:01:03.732 --> 00:01:08.652
The aim is to create conditions where people can build durable understanding and usable skill.

00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:11.604
This does not require every course to be elaborate.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:15.868
Even a short module can be stronger when it states a performance goal,

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:19.804
uses a concrete example, asks learners to retrieve or apply the idea,

00:01:19.804 --> 00:01:22.100
and gives feedback that points to improvement.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.036
The discipline is to spend course time on the things most likely

00:01:26.036 --> 00:01:28.660
to change what the learner can do afterward.
